# Sync Colab notebooks (read-only mirror)

Invoke with `@sync-colab-notebooks`. Run the workflow; do not only describe it.

**Goal:** Refresh the local read-only notebook mirror from GitHub and record the exact synced commit SHA in this repo for agent context.

**Source of truth:** `https://github.com/marcory-hub/Seeed_Grove_Vision_AI_Module_V2` (branch `main`; Colab "Open in Colab" target)
**Not this repo:** `yolo11n-on-grove-vision-ai-v2` (legacy notebook mirror; stale since 2026-03)
**Firmware submodule:** `gv2_firmware/` is the same GitHub repo on branch `yolo11-vespa`; do not use it for notebook sync.
**Local mirror path:** `colab-notebooks/` (gitignored in this repo)

## Workflow

### 0) Preflight
- Confirm repo root: `vespa_smart_trap`.
- Check whether `colab-notebooks/.git` exists.

### 1) Ensure local mirror exists
If missing, clone `main` locally (read-only use in this repo):
```sh
git clone --branch main https://github.com/marcory-hub/Seeed_Grove_Vision_AI_Module_V2 colab-notebooks
```

If present, continue.

### 2) Sync latest notebook changes
```sh
git -C colab-notebooks fetch origin
git -C colab-notebooks checkout main
git -C colab-notebooks pull --ff-only origin main
```

If `pull --ff-only` fails: stop and report the error.

### 3) Record synced version for agent visibility
Write a tracked pointer file:
```sh
mkdir -p docs
printf "repo: https://github.com/marcory-hub/Seeed_Grove_Vision_AI_Module_V2\nbranch: main\nsha: %s\ndate: %s\n" \
"$(git -C colab-notebooks rev-parse HEAD)" \
"$(date +%F)" > docs/notebook_source_of_truth.md
```

### 4) Report result
Show:
- `git -C colab-notebooks rev-parse --short HEAD`
- `git -C colab-notebooks log -1 --oneline`
- root notebooks: `YOLO11n_training_2026_02_19.ipynb`, `YOLO_pt_to_vela_2026_02_24.ipynb`
- `docs/notebook_source_of_truth.md` contents

## Done when
- Local notebook mirror is up to date with `origin/main`.
- `docs/notebook_source_of_truth.md` reflects the latest synced SHA and date.
